<item>
  <title>
    <![CDATA[  Exploring Catala  ]]>
  </title>
  <link> https://jacobzelko.com/notes/aaa-0287/index.html </link>
  <guid> https://jacobzelko.com/notes/aaa-0287/index.html </guid>
  <description>
    <![CDATA[  An exploration of the Catala language to explore how to encode exceptions  ]]>
  </description>  
  
  <content:encoded>
    <![CDATA[  
<link rel="stylesheet" href="aaa-0287.css">
<h3 class="sectionHead"><span class="titlemark">1   </span><a id="x1-10001"></a>Exploring Catala</h3><div class="flushleft"><p class="noindent"><span class="cmbx-10">Keywords: </span>law, catala
</p></div><p class="noindent"><span class="cmbx-10">Summary: </span>An exploration of the Catala language to explore how to encode
exceptions
</p><p class="noindent">Per the <a href="https://catala-lang.org">Catala language website</a>:
</p><blockquote><p class="noindent"><span class="cmti-10">Catala  is  a  domain-specific  language  designed  by  researchers  in</span><span class="cmti-10">Computer  Science  and  Law,  for  precisely  deriving  algorithms</span><span class="cmti-10">producing automated legal decisions.</span></p><footer></footer></blockquote><h4 class="subsectionHead"><span class="titlemark">1.1   </span><a id="x1-20001.1"></a>Introductory Catala Code</h4><p class="noindent">This Catala program is copied directly from the documentation of Catala and is the
“hello world” of Catala. It outputs the integer <img alt="42  " class="math" src="aaa-0287-d25e1211386494455a2cc605710dc600.svg"></img> as the Answer to the Ultimate
Question of Life, the Universe, and Everything:
</p><p class="noindent"></p><div class="minted-block" data-lang="catala_en"><p></p><pre class="fancyvrb" id="fancyvrb1"><a id="x1-2002r1"></a><span class="cmtt-10">declaration</span><span class="cmtt-10"> scope</span><span class="cmtt-10"> HelloWorld:</span> 
<a id="x1-2004r2"></a><span class="cmtt-10"> </span><span class="cmtt-10"> output</span><span class="cmtt-10"> answer_everything</span><span class="cmtt-10"> content</span><span class="cmtt-10"> integer</span> 
<a id="x1-2006r3"></a> 
<a id="x1-2008r4"></a><span class="cmtt-10">scope</span><span class="cmtt-10"> HelloWorld:</span> 
<a id="x1-2010r5"></a><span class="cmtt-10"> </span><span class="cmtt-10"> definition</span><span class="cmtt-10"> answer_everything</span><span class="cmtt-10"> equals</span><span class="cmtt-10"> 42</span></pre><p class="noindent"></p></div><p></p><blockquote><p class="noindent"><span class="cmti-10">Interestingly, this section of code comes from a tex file! Catala is</span><span class="cmti-10">built around literate programming and this section is actually a valid</span><span class="cmti-10">Catala file.</span></p><footer></footer></blockquote><h2 id="how_to_cite">How To Cite</h2>
<p>Zelko, Jacob S. <em>Exploring Catala</em>. <a href="https://jacobzelko.com/notes/aaa-0287/">https://jacobzelko.com/notes/aaa-0287/</a>. August 24, 2026.</p>
